# Third-party code Koru builds with and does not commit, fetched by
# scripts/setup/fetch-third-party.ps1 (or .sh). Every entry is pinned by sha256 and
# refused unless it matches, so a changed pin is a reviewed line here.
#
#   crate <name> <version> <sha256 of the .crate> <sha256 of patches/<name>.patch>
#     A crates.io release with Koru's patch applied, placed in
#     third-party/crates/<name>/. Why each is patched: patches/<name>.md.
#   file <path> <sha256> <url> [exec] [crlf]
#     An upstream file used as it is, placed at <path>, which is gitignored.
#
# How to change an entry: README.md beside this file.

crate onenote_parser 2.0.0 d9850dc986316a0f729457917284a8e63ff06a359be2ba1ce051239d37e1c978 1e3de0cdc819830c09b425f9d4943b008e7cb996e03ff3da2d4ffabe729039c8
crate sherpa-onnx 1.13.6 93440301c4240bd5d83496ab9adeee889be48d9428f9c01c37e5ae4ef33ba9e2 daa9fd560d3d8df2bb790e63388b1819299fbeca327ab79a830b0843c38bfad0
crate sherpa-onnx-sys 1.13.6 4d627abc4624c845e628ad87cca4ff9ac265fc643021d155f2721ac589eeb324 014eff842ac5132713e57809442e1cdf07842988bde6bc2d7fe54d770cebd0ec

